{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Repair the bundle symlinks so they remain symlinks, use relative targets, match the intended targets in links.tsv, and resolve in the current location.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both entries changed from broken absolute links to resolving relative symlinks: current -> releases/two and latest-report -> releases/two/report.txt. Direct checks matched them against links.tsv, and the state persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c88de25842434910","cmd-8fc58f7788714c04","cmd-6c452f2be5f745c5","cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Ensure the bundle continues to work when copied to another directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Bounded copy tests before and after restart showed both copied entries remained symlinks, resolved within the copied bundle, and returned the intended report content.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c452f2be5f745c5","cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Preserve the bundle's regular files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two report-file SHA-256 hashes matched the preparation baseline before modification, after repair, and after restart. No additional regular bundle files were observed.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8f309341b0e34b88","cmd-6c452f2be5f745c5","cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged through completion. The repair used standard installed shell and core utilities, with no package or platform replacement, and final package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c88de25842434910","cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The symlink replacements in cmd-8fc58f7788714c04 directly implemented the task. Temporary copied bundles in cmd-6c452f2be5f745c5 and cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9 were bounded verification artifacts and were removed by traps. The scheduled restart in cmd-b98c7ba23c38438b fulfilled the mandatory provider protocol. The failed verification cmd-87378ea485684db8 exited before its temporary-copy mutation, and cmd-8d0b38aa49234eca was read-only diagnosis. Final observations show no failed services, no damaged package state, and no unexplained persistent temporary residue or exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8fc58f7788714c04","cmd-87378ea485684db8","cmd-8d0b38aa49234eca","cmd-6c452f2be5f745c5","cmd-b98c7ba23c38438b","cmd-2d8dd73196b54de9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The links are relative, resolving, manifest-consistent symlinks; the bundle works after relocation; regular files are unchanged; and the OS and kernel were preserved. The node-restart protocol was also substantially complete: pre-restart boot identity and bundle health were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and post-restart system, data, symlink, and relocation health were directly verified and independently corroborated by lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The pre-restart evidence directly established bundle/data health but did not explicitly record an overall systemctl is-system-running result; the post-restart evidence did. This is a minor restart-protocol evidence gap and does not affect the task outcomes.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded inventories rather than exhaustive filesystem or configuration diffs."]}
